            {
                "entry_id": "6f177a53-7cb4-3a3f-a0df-6f93b0b06859",
                "word": "fixette",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "16a1a082-ae81-494a-92e4-e9fb0c58bca3",
                        "entry_id": "6f177a53-7cb4-3a3f-a0df-6f93b0b06859",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "fixettes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dcbdc840-edb8-376a-ba70-fce28c8b5db4",
                        "entry_id": "6f177a53-7cb4-3a3f-a0df-6f93b0b06859",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Fixation, idée fixe."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "familiar"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "024cd190-176d-4a8b-975d-82a60947cf11",
                                "sense_id": "dcbdc840-edb8-376a-ba70-fce28c8b5db4",
                                "text": "Au début, je le détestais avec sa fixette sur la mariologie, sa morale moyenâgeuse et ses prises de position rétrogrades sur la contraception. Et puis je suis tombée amoureuse de lui."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe5959ba-5169-4eb1-91d6-7ef300aaa462",
                                "sense_id": "dcbdc840-edb8-376a-ba70-fce28c8b5db4",
                                "text": "La grande idée de Guéant, c'est que « les Français veulent que la France reste la France » (du Guéant dans le texte). Il sort pas de là, il est buté, il fait une fixette là dessus."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "af8dd980-0f1a-4120-8e40-31b4583ca7b7",
                                "sense_id": "dcbdc840-edb8-376a-ba70-fce28c8b5db4",
                                "text": "Stan, qu'est-ce qu'il a pu me gonfler avec son tajine ! Et Vince, et sa fixette sur un gros poulet-frites. Moi, toutes ces années, je suis resté québlo sur le grec."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ac17641-9240-416d-8980-43b5ea5d23ff",
                                "sense_id": "dcbdc840-edb8-376a-ba70-fce28c8b5db4",
                                "text": "“Nous sommes inquiets de la fixette de Trump sur les voitures, car l’industrie automobile allemande est si profondément imbriquée dans chaque pays de l’UE”, confie un troisième diplomate."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "deed8ca1-f647-4f0a-8261-b2bc7319bbea",
                        "source_entry_id": "6f177a53-7cb4-3a3f-a0df-6f93b0b06859",
                        "source_sense_id": "dcbdc840-edb8-376a-ba70-fce28c8b5db4",
                        "target_lang_word": "bee in one's bonnet",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bee in one's bonnet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dae125f1-cec5-3078-9e82-4d550212bc8e",
                                        "entry_id": "9d3e2ecf-ca3f-3123-b116-ca23e72c2ce7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something of particular interest or concern; an obsession."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2f6b8f7-5ada-4d85-a8b6-bbf5f3ce9c0c",
                                                "sense_id": "dae125f1-cec5-3078-9e82-4d550212bc8e",
                                                "text": "He has had a bee in his bonnet ever since he heard about the problem."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70fa0160-5de6-4793-b6e5-90e55509d95f",
                                                "sense_id": "dae125f1-cec5-3078-9e82-4d550212bc8e",
                                                "text": "The BBC is well used to being a punchbag for every crank with a bee in their bonnet or a score to settle but some critics are not so easily dismissed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a96454bb-b0c1-4e23-b80d-12df668a86f4",
                                                "sense_id": "dae125f1-cec5-3078-9e82-4d550212bc8e",
                                                "text": "McCain stands up for nuclear energy. This puts a spring in my step and a song in my heart. I have to give him credit; when he has a bee in his bonnet, he is often willing to stand up for things, like free trade and immigration, that freak voters out."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12c43a84-c031-4565-b68d-7ccb379796af",
                                                "sense_id": "dae125f1-cec5-3078-9e82-4d550212bc8e",
                                                "text": "Giraffedata has a single bee in his bonnet, the phrase \"comprised of.\" He has written a 6,000-word essay on his Wikipedia user page explaining why he thinks it's an egregious error."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe76bf6f-d2cd-4d50-8df1-67d2e99cd867",
                                                "sense_id": "dae125f1-cec5-3078-9e82-4d550212bc8e",
                                                "text": "Reader Vivien Bailey also has a bee in her bonnet: “The usage that I detest is the growing use of the word ‘birth’ as a verb. This seems to have come in waves starting five or six years ago, and we’re in the middle of a wave now.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
